Z||000000||Hybrid2M6||11-23-2001||01:19 PM||||You got it, just like on Mr2's 2 lid's in back. One for the trunk, and one for the engine.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dc3-trunk.jpg"> <BR>I'm thinking about modifying the engine vents, just to make my fiero that much more different. Maybe just adding a custom style vent in between the existing two.(Insert ideas here; wink, wink.) I was thinking about using the factory decklid release switch to open the new trunk, since it will be accessed more often than the engine bay. (Hopefully) And for the engine lid, using two racing "hood" pin to hold it down and then a locking style "hood" pin that comes with a key. I know I have a lot of work ahead of me in this project, but it will be worth it. I'm sure I'm not the only one here that has been mollywhopped on the back of the head while tending to ole Duke. This should reduce that and hopefully the lid struts I will be installing will prevent that all together. Any ideas would be helpfull before I dig in. <P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/customgfx.jpg"> <BR>1986 SE IronDuke<BR>Adjustable Touring Wing<BR>American Racing Carrera's<BR> -225/50VR16 Falken Ziex 502<BR> -225/45ZR17 Falken Azenis<BR>Cleared and Painted(red) Tail lights||||reg||6
